<title>USA: Melville Corp elects Fleet's Murray to board.</title>
<headline>Melville Corp elects Fleet's Murray to board.</headline>
<dateline>WOONSOCKET, R.I. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Melville Corp said on Monday that Terrence Murray has been elected to its board, increasing its size to 13 members.</p>
<p>Murray, 57, is president and chief executive officer of Fleet Financial Group, a position he has held since 1982.</p>
<p>Fleet Financial, headquartered in Boston, is the 11th largest bank holding company in the United States, with about $88 billion in assets, a statement from Melville said.</p>
